# Prompt and matrix source merge (mandatory)

**Never hand-edit generated artifacts.** Edit sources under `tools/`, then rebuild before ending the task.

## Agent workflow (every applicable task)

1. Edit source file(s) in `tools/` (or matrix JSON).
2. **Run merge** before marking work complete:
   ```bash
   python tools/merge_all.py
   ```
3. If only prompt `.txt` changed (no JSON): `python tools/merge_suno_v2_prompt.py` is acceptable.
4. When the user asks for a commit: stage **sources + generated outputs** together.

**Do not skip merge** after changing any file listed below. Leaving generated Dart/Python out of sync is a ship blocker.

## Generated outputs (do not edit by hand)

| Source | Generated |
|--------|-----------|
| `tools/suno_v2_system_prompt_body.txt` (preferred) or modular `tools/*.txt` in `merge_suno_v2_prompt.py` chain | `lib/core/constants/suno_system_prompt_v2_candidate.dart`, `elite_human_lyricist_directive.dart`, `server/app/suno_system_prompt_v2.py` |
| `tools/songwriter/**` (modules, stages, JSON configs) | `lib/core/constants/songwriter_prompts_data.dart`, `server/app/songwriter/prompts_data.py` |
| `tools/drum_matrix.json` | `lib/core/utils/drum_matrix_data.dart` |
| `tools/genre_fx_matrix.json` | `lib/core/utils/genre_fx_matrix_data.dart` |
| `tools/live_instrument_matrix.json` | `lib/core/utils/live_instrument_matrix_data.dart` |
| `tools/code_translation_matrix.json` | `lib/core/utils/code_translation_matrix_data.dart` |
| `tools/genre_hardware_profiles_v2_1.json` | `lib/data/generated/genre_hardware_profiles_data.dart` (consumer: `lib/services/genre_hardware_profiles.dart`) |

## Hand-edited in parallel (no merge — keep Python/Dart in sync manually)

| Area | Files |
|------|-------|
| Runtime user-block injectors | `server/app/*.py`, `lib/core/utils/*.dart`, `lib/core/constants/genre_lyrics_directives.dart` |
| Lyric masters (read at runtime) | `tools/lyrics_training/*_master.txt`, `*_template.txt` |
| Flutter UI / models | `lib/presentation/**`, `lib/data/models/**` |

When changing runtime injectors **and** canonical `tools/*.txt` spec for the same feature, update **both** and run `merge_all.py` for the tools side.

## Merge entrypoint

```bash
python tools/merge_all.py
```

See `tools/README.md` and `docs/CREATION_PIPELINE.md` for full merge order.
